<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · movement</p><h1 class="enc-title">Czechoslovak New Wave</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1960s</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Czechoslovak New Wave was a movement of young film-makers in the 1960s, among them Miloš Forman, Věra Chytilová and Jiří Menzel. Using irony, improvisation and experiment, their films questioned the official culture of communist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a>. The Shop on Main Street and Closely Watched Trains won Academy Awards, and the movement ended with the crushing of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-spring">Prague Spring</a>.</p></div>
